1
00:00:03,200 --> 00:00:08,038
KING GENIUS: There are two wisdoms,
constructor. One acts, and one refrains.

2
00:00:08,078 --> 00:00:12,314
The greater refrains, for no mind
can see where its acts will end.

3
00:00:13,414 --> 00:00:18,622
TRURL: To refrain from acting, you must
first be able to act. Inaction is certain.

4
00:00:18,662 --> 00:00:20,902
That is all it has to recommend it.

5
00:00:22,502 --> 00:00:25,375
KING GENIUS: Then let your
machines act. The white one first.

6
00:00:26,975 --> 00:00:29,178
THE WHITE MACHINE: This
is a story Trurl once

7
00:00:29,218 --> 00:00:31,361
told a king who wanted
stories without end.

8
00:00:35,361 --> 00:00:38,308
King Zipperupus had a
courtier who wished him dead.

9
00:00:38,348 --> 00:00:42,213
The courtier brought him cabinets
of dreams that dream themselves.

10
00:00:42,913 --> 00:00:46,945
Whoever plugs into one cannot tell
the dream from the waking world.

11
00:00:48,145 --> 00:00:49,419
ZIPPERUPUS: Then let me dream.

12
00:00:55,019 --> 00:00:56,744
Stand aside. Let me pass.

13
00:00:57,344 --> 00:00:58,927
THE GATEKEEPER: Ten ducats.

14
00:00:59,427 --> 00:01:01,405
ZIPPERUPUS: Ten ducats, for one embrace?

15
00:01:01,905 --> 00:01:03,900
THE GATEKEEPER: Not a ducat less.

16
00:01:04,300 --> 00:01:05,478
ZIPPERUPUS: Then you get nothing!

17
00:01:08,078 --> 00:01:10,244
Is this a dream, or am I awake?

18
00:01:16,644 --> 00:01:19,205
THE WHITE MACHINE: Every exit
led him back to the same room.

19
00:01:29,805 --> 00:01:31,554
KING GENIUS: Clever.
Have you nothing darker?

20
00:01:32,354 --> 00:01:34,168
TRURL: The black one, Your Majesty.

21
00:01:36,968 --> 00:01:41,112
THE BLACK MACHINE: In the Constellation
of the Wringer there was a spiral galaxy,

22
00:01:41,612 --> 00:01:44,498
and in the galaxy, a black nebula,

23
00:01:44,998 --> 00:01:47,705
and in the nebula, five clusters,

24
00:01:48,205 --> 00:01:52,699
and in the fifth cluster, a
lilac sun, very old and very dim,

25
00:01:53,199 --> 00:01:56,086
and its third planet had two moons,

26
00:01:56,586 --> 00:01:59,318
and on the second moon
there was a garbage dump,

27
00:01:59,358 --> 00:02:01,668
where nothing ever happened but garbage.

28
00:02:04,068 --> 00:02:09,150
One day Trurl, flying past, threw an
old cracked jug out of his window.

29
00:02:11,750 --> 00:02:14,993
It struck a can, the can bent
round a wire, a current ran,

30
00:02:15,033 --> 00:02:18,260
and in the middle of the dump,
by accident, a mind began.

31
00:02:22,060 --> 00:02:25,536
MYMOSH: Look at me. I am perfect.
How good must be the one who made me!

32
00:02:28,936 --> 00:02:32,331
THE BLACK MACHINE: On the seventh
step he tripped, fell on his head,

33
00:02:32,371 --> 00:02:35,200
and lay in the garbage for
three hundred thousand years.

34
00:02:39,200 --> 00:02:40,475
MYMOSH: Apparently... I am.

35
00:02:41,475 --> 00:02:45,467
THE BLACK MACHINE: His eyes had rusted
away. All he could do now was think.

36
00:02:47,067 --> 00:02:50,655
MYMOSH: If there is nothing outside
me, I will think a world inside.

37
00:02:56,255 --> 00:02:58,477
THE BLACK MACHINE: He
called it the Gozmos.

38
00:02:58,517 --> 00:03:01,211
He gave it kind laws, where
nothing ever had to end,

39
00:03:01,251 --> 00:03:03,513
and he felt responsible
for everyone in it.

40
00:03:04,913 --> 00:03:08,585
Last of all he imagined two
travelers, Baucis and Ondragor,

41
00:03:08,625 --> 00:03:11,204
walking hand in hand among his dark suns.

42
00:03:17,404 --> 00:03:21,886
A shard of that same jug drifted
across the puddle toward his head.

43
00:03:29,086 --> 00:03:32,655
And those who had made him
never learned that he was gone.

44
00:03:40,255 --> 00:03:44,261
KING GENIUS: I will pay you,
constructor. I give you your life.

45
00:03:44,301 --> 00:03:48,925
Go, and keep hiding truths too bitter
for this world inside fairy tales.

46
00:03:50,325 --> 00:03:53,076
TRURL: My life? Was that
to have been my payment?

47
00:03:55,276 --> 00:03:56,278
KING GENIUS: Tell me another.

